From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: ps3fb: restrict the GPU ioctls to root and copy their arguments

OtherOS++'s ps3/0030 gave ps3fb a direct GPU interface for GPU research
tools: the PS3GPU_IOCTL_* calls on /dev/fbN and the /dev/ps3gpu_*
mappings of the GPU's memory, FIFO and control areas. Keep it for those
tools, run as root, and close it to everyone else:

- PS3GPU_IOCTL_INFO, _ENTER and _EXIT, and opening /dev/ps3gpu_*, need
  CAP_SYS_ADMIN (-EPERM otherwise). /dev/fbN and its other ioctls stay
  as they are for the console, X and ps3-video-mode.
- ENTER and EXIT copy their int argument in with get_user() and take
  only 0 (-EINVAL otherwise). A second ENTER gets -EBUSY, an EXIT
  without an ENTER -EINVAL, an EXIT from another process -EPERM.
- The set-attribute, set-context-attribute and cursor ioctls (9 to 14)
  are removed: nothing uses them. ps3fb answers them like any unknown
  ioctl (-ENOTTY). Their structs leave the uapi header, and the numbers
  stay reserved.
- Between ENTER and EXIT, ps3fb skips its own blits and flips (the
  console, a mode change, FSEL, the last close), checked under
  ps3_gpu_mutex, which ENTER sets the flag under. ENTER no longer stops
  ps3fb's blit thread or unmaps its FIFO control area, so it doesn't
  wait on the thread while holding the fb_info lock, and EXIT is the
  reset program under ps3_gpu_mutex.
- A session also ends by itself when the process that entered is gone:
  checked after each close of /dev/fbN or /dev/ps3gpu_* (also when no
  file has /dev/fbN open any more), at the next ENTER and at a takeover.
  A probe killed after ENTER no longer leaves the console without
  updates and the RSX driver's takeover refused.

The RSX driver (ps3rsx) doesn't use any of these: it shares the GPU
through the in-kernel API (ps3fb_gpu_takeover() and the rest), which
keeps working; its takeover is refused only during a live session, as
before.

The /dev/ps3gpu_* file operations get an owner (ps3fb is built in, so
it changes nothing today) and are const.

Forwarded: no
